# Nibs — agentic-first issue tracker

Track ALL work in this project with nibs (issues stored as Markdown files), not
TodoWrite or ad-hoc todo lists.

**Learn the CLI grammar first: run `nibs cheat` once.** It prints the whole
verb surface (get/list/rel, new/set/body/mv/rm/close, catalog) on one screen.
For detail: `nibs catalog <topic>` (fields, filters, hierarchy, recipes,
examples, schema) and `nibs <cmd> --help`. Full reference: `nibs prime --full`.
Do not guess syntax — read the grammar first.

## Workflow

- BEFORE a task: find or create a nib (`nibs list --ready`, `nibs new "Title" -t <type>`), set it `in-progress` (`nibs set <id> -s in-progress`). `--ready` excludes blocked, in-progress, completed, scrapped, draft, and deferred/parked nibs.
- DURING: keep the body's todo items current (`- [ ]` → `- [x]`) as work happens (`nibs body <id> --replace-old … --replace-new …`).
- AFTER: mark `completed` only when no unchecked todos remain. Prefer `nibs close <id> --summary -` (appends a summary, propagates to the parent). When scrapping, add a `## Reasons for Scrapping` section: `nibs body <id> --section "## Reasons for Scrapping" --set - --create` (upsert), or `--append`.
- COMMITS: include both code and nib files.
- SUBAGENTS: set `in-progress` BEFORE launching, `completed` AFTER — they run fresh and won't update nibs for you.

## Errors

Every command uses stable exit codes (0 ok / 2 validation / 3 not-found / 4 conflict / 5 io); with `--json`, errors come back as `{"error":{"code","message"}}`. If a `nibs` command errors, STOP. Find the root cause and suggest a mitigation (code fix, follow-up nib, workaround). Never silently retry.
</EXTREMELY_IMPORTANT>
